lso been unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it, and review why it was promoted to production after failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 16971, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TGFARubeJUwsujox27zWt7", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16971, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TGFARubeJUwsujox27zWt7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20915, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and passing health checks again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What went wrong:** checkout-api v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause before redeploying v2.3.1, and review why it reached production. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CV8GKb28Bdtbj