r failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and passing health checks again. I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What went wrong:** checkout-api v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It also lists two follow-ups: find the root cause before redeploying v2.3.1, and review why it reached production. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}